<?xml version='1.0'?>
<!--
  The room around the arena: the event tent the UCF Exolith Lab regolith bin
  sits under, a concrete floor, and the team pit, mission-control desk, judges'
  table and people standing round the walls.

  Same frame as perseus_arc_world (guidebook Origin Point, +X east, +Y north).
  Nothing here is inside the regolith bin: the arena's outer wall faces are
  X +-4.72, Y -0.15 .. 9.10 (judge platform included), and every prop keeps
  out of that box, so the rover can't reach any of it.

  SENSOR-VISIBLE ON PURPOSE, unlike lunabotics_zones. A real lidar sees the
  tent and the people round the walls, so the sim does too:

    - The canopy: eave 3.0 m, ridge 5.5 m. The MID-360's +52 deg rays hit it
      from about 2.5 m out. Both traversability nodes drop returns more than
      max_sensor_height_m (1.5 m) above the lidar, which is exactly what that
      filter is for; LIO gets the extra structure.
    - Everything at floor level is behind the 0.85 m walls, which are already
      lethal in the costmaps.

  The canopy and its frame cast no shadows. Under a real tent the bin is lit by
  the tent lights, not the sun; letting the roof shadow the sun would leave the
  whole bed on ambient light only and starve the D455 the fiducials depend on.

  Props are OpenRobotics Fuel models, fetched once and cached in ~/.gz/fuel
  like the Falling Rock boulders. The tent, floor and small fittings are
  primitives. meshes/tent_canopy.obj is generated: roof, gables and valance,
  every face wound to face INTO the tent only. ogre2 culls back faces, so the
  rover's lidar and cameras underneath see the canopy, while the Gazebo GUI
  looking down from outside sees straight through it to the arena. (The GUI
  camera has no visibility mask to hide it with, unlike the sensors.) Zoom the
  GUI camera in under the eave and the canopy shows again.
-->
<sdf version='1.8'>
  <model name='exolith_lab'>
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
    <static>true</static>

    <!-- Concrete floor round the bin, top at grade (z = 0). Four slabs leave a hole for the bin itself. -->
    <link name='floor_s'>
      <pose>0.0000 -3.5750 -0.0500 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000</pose>
      <collision name='floor_s_collision'><geometry><box><size>22.000 6.850 0.100</size></box></geometry></collision>
      <visual name='floor_s_visual'><geometry><box><size>22.000 6.850 0.100</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.42 0.42 0.40 1</ambient><diffuse>0.52 0.52 0.50 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material></visual>
    </link>
    <link name='floor_n'>
      <pose>0.0000 12.5500 -0.0500 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000</pose>
      <collision name='floor_n_collision'><geometry><box><size>22.000 6.900 0.100</size></box></geometry></collision>
      <visual name='floor_n_visual'><geometry><box><size>22.000 6.900 0.100</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.42 0.42 0.40 1</ambient><diffuse>0.52 0.52 0.50 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material></visual>
    </link>
    <link name='floor_w'>
